1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,866
Between India and Tibet, there is

2
00:00:02,916 --> 00:00:05,253
a kingdom that measures happiness.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,715
This is Bhutan, known as the

4
00:00:07,765 --> 00:00:09,609
Land of the Thunder Dragon.

5
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:12,260
Its capital is Thimphu.

6
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:17,317
About seven hundred ninety-three thousand people live

7
00:00:17,367 --> 00:00:20,882
here, on thirty-eight thousand square kilometers.

8
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:22,732
They speak Dzongkha.

9
00:00:22,782 --> 00:00:24,863
In Dzongkha, hello is Kuzu zangpo la.

10
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,393
And they pay with the ngultrum.

11
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,261
A few things that might surprise you.

12
00:00:32,311 --> 00:00:33,875
And stay until the end, for

13
00:00:33,925 --> 00:00:35,608
a mystery nobody ever solved.

14
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:41,688
Bhutan measures success with Gross National Happiness, an idea

15
00:00:41,738 --> 00:00:45,423
introduced by its fourth king in nineteen seventy-two.

16
00:00:45,973 --> 00:00:47,468
It is carbon negative.

17
00:00:47,518 --> 00:00:51,119
Forests cover most of the land, and the constitution

18
00:00:51,169 --> 00:00:54,279
says at least sixty percent must stay forest.

19
00:00:54,829 --> 00:00:57,765
And Thimphu, the capital, has no traffic lights.

20
00:00:57,815 --> 00:01:00,254
Police officers direct the cars by hand.

21
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,408
Some places most tourists miss.

22
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:07,862
The Tiger's Nest monastery clings to a cliff

23
00:01:07,912 --> 00:01:10,766
about nine hundred meters above the Paro valley.

24
00:01:10,816 --> 00:01:12,883
It was built in sixteen ninety-two.

25
00:01:13,433 --> 00:01:15,708
Punakha Dzong sits where two rivers meet,

26
00:01:15,758 --> 00:01:17,467
and it is often called the most

27
00:01:17,517 --> 00:01:19,395
beautiful fortress in the country.

28
00:01:19,945 --> 00:01:23,629
In the Phobjika valley, rare black-necked cranes arrive from

29
00:01:23,679 --> 00:01:26,802
Tibet every winter, from late October to mid March.

30
00:01:27,352 --> 00:01:30,472
And Chimi Lakhang, built in fourteen ninety-nine,

31
00:01:30,522 --> 00:01:33,124
is the fertility temple, honoring a saint

32
00:01:33,174 --> 00:01:34,871
known as the Divine Madman.

33
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:37,511
Time to spend ten dollars.

34
00:01:39,350 --> 00:01:40,511
A simple meal at a cheap

35
00:01:40,561 --> 00:01:42,379
restaurant costs about three dollars.

36
00:01:42,929 --> 00:01:45,425
A bottle of Coke costs about fifty cents.

37
00:01:45,975 --> 00:01:47,092
A half liter of local

38
00:01:47,142 --> 00:01:48,648
beer costs about one dollar.

39
00:01:49,198 --> 00:01:50,429
And a taxi ride starts

40
00:01:50,479 --> 00:01:51,827
at less than one dollar.

41
00:01:52,377 --> 00:01:54,838
So ten dollars covers a meal, a Coke,

42
00:01:54,888 --> 00:01:56,874
a beer, and a short taxi ride.

43
00:01:56,924 --> 00:01:59,589
But the real cost is the government fee:

44
00:01:59,639 --> 00:02:02,440
one hundred dollars per person, per night.

45
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,225
Careful, some rules matter here.

46
00:02:07,050 --> 00:02:09,644
Don't smoke in public or near religious sites.

47
00:02:09,694 --> 00:02:12,862
Tobacco sales are tightly controlled, and foreigners who

48
00:02:12,912 --> 00:02:15,046
sell it can be charged with smuggling.

49
00:02:15,596 --> 00:02:18,713
Don't take photos inside temples or sacred rooms.

50
00:02:18,763 --> 00:02:20,070
Ask your guide first.

51
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:23,088
Don't litter, and don't harm protected animals.

52
00:02:23,138 --> 00:02:25,445
Littering is illegal everywhere, and hurting

53
00:02:25,495 --> 00:02:27,267
protected species can mean prison.

54
00:02:27,817 --> 00:02:29,037
Don't take antiques home.

55
00:02:29,087 --> 00:02:30,104
It is illegal to take

56
00:02:30,154 --> 00:02:31,324
them out of the country.

57
00:02:31,874 --> 00:02:33,792
And don't try to climb a mountain.

58
00:02:33,842 --> 00:02:35,817
Mountaineering is banned in Bhutan.

59
00:02:36,767 --> 00:02:38,829
Food, clothes, and music.

60
00:02:40,617 --> 00:02:43,406
The national dish is ema datshi, chilies

61
00:02:43,456 --> 00:02:46,175
cooked in cheese, served with red rice.

62
00:02:46,725 --> 00:02:48,841
Men wear the go, a knee-length

63
00:02:48,891 --> 00:02:50,430
robe tied with a belt.

64
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:54,185
Women wear the keera, a wrapped, ankle-length dress.

65
00:02:54,735 --> 00:02:57,948
And the traditional instrument is the dranyen, a long

66
00:02:57,998 --> 00:03:00,596
lute topped with a carved sea monster head.

67
00:03:01,533 --> 00:03:02,396
Let's rewind.

68
00:03:04,217 --> 00:03:07,613
Between sixteen sixteen and sixteen thirty-four, a

69
00:03:07,663 --> 00:03:10,990
monk named Ngawang Namgyal, called the Zhabdrung,

70
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:13,333
united the valleys into one state.

71
00:03:13,883 --> 00:03:15,616
Then came nineteen oh seven.

72
00:03:15,666 --> 00:03:19,183
Ugyen Wangchuck was chosen as the first hereditary king.

73
00:03:19,733 --> 00:03:21,662
Fast forward to two thousand eight.

74
00:03:21,712 --> 00:03:23,528
Bhutan got its first constitution

75
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:25,620
and became a parliamentary democracy.

76
00:03:26,567 --> 00:03:28,747
And now, the chapter you were

77
00:03:28,797 --> 00:03:31,745
all waiting for: legends and mysteries.

78
00:03:33,583 --> 00:03:36,335
Legend says that in the eighth century,

79
00:03:36,385 --> 00:03:39,208
the master Guru Rinpoche flew from Tibet

80
00:03:39,258 --> 00:03:41,004
on the back of a tigress.

81
00:03:41,054 --> 00:03:44,453
She was his consort, Yeshe Tsogyal, transformed.

82
00:03:44,503 --> 00:03:46,823
He landed on a steep cliff in the

83
00:03:46,873 --> 00:03:49,697
Paro valley, and meditated in a cave for

84
00:03:49,747 --> 00:03:53,145
three years, three months, three days, and three

85
00:03:53,195 --> 00:03:56,163
hours, to subdue the demons of the valley.

86
00:03:56,213 --> 00:03:59,180
Centuries later, a temple was built there.

87
00:03:59,230 --> 00:04:01,838
Today, it is called the Tiger's Nest.

88
00:04:02,388 --> 00:04:05,255
Then there is the migoi, the yeti of Bhutan.

89
00:04:05,305 --> 00:04:08,038
In the far east, the Sakteng sanctuary was

90
00:04:08,088 --> 00:04:10,955
created partly to protect its supposed home.

91
00:04:11,005 --> 00:04:14,335
Many locals strongly believe in it, and Bhutan even

92
00:04:14,385 --> 00:04:17,650
issued stamps honoring it in the nineteen sixties.

93
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:20,765
But science has never confirmed that it exists.

94
00:04:21,315 --> 00:04:23,170
And finally, Gangkar Puensum.

95
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:26,389
At seven thousand five hundred seventy meters, it

96
00:04:26,439 --> 00:04:29,214
is the highest unclimbed mountain on Earth.

97
00:04:29,264 --> 00:04:32,104
Expeditions failed in the nineteen eighties.

98
00:04:32,154 --> 00:04:36,440
In nineteen ninety-four, Bhutan banned climbing above six thousand

99
00:04:36,490 --> 00:04:39,593
meters, out of respect for local beliefs, and in

100
00:04:39,643 --> 00:04:42,747
two thousand three it banned all mountaineering.

101
00:04:42,797 --> 00:04:45,309
Its border with China is also disputed.

102
00:04:45,359 --> 00:04:47,411
So nobody has ever stood on top.

103
00:04:50,667 --> 00:04:51,626
That was Bhutan.

104
00:04:51,676 --> 00:04:53,832
Which country should we visit next?

105
00:04:53,882 --> 00:04:55,345
Tell me in the comments.

